// Single-action schema, window-expiry flavor: a self-referential
// `previous` with a tight 30s window and a trace whose
// gaps straddle it — so the false verdicts come from WINDOW EXPIRY, not
// from a field-pin mismatch (all events are alice's).
//
// Trace gaps: @0 -> @10 (10s) -> @100 (90s) -> @120 (20s).
// tp0: no previous timepoint            -> false
// tp1: gap 10s <= 30s                   -> true
// tp2: gap 90s  > 30s (window expired)  -> false
// tp3: gap 20s <= 30s                   -> true

permit (
    principal,
    action == Drupe::Action::"Transfer",
    resource
)
when temporal {
    previous within 30s Drupe::Action::"Transfer"::request{ input.user: context.input.user }
};
